Whatever you don't use, you lose.

1318
00:52:29,962 --> 00:52:31,962
Lack of use causes loss.

1319
00:52:37,962 --> 00:52:38,962
On this planet.

1320
00:52:38,962 --> 00:52:41,962
Maybe not the next one, but on this one.

1321
00:52:41,962 --> 00:52:43,462
If you tie your arm to

1322
00:52:43,462 --> 00:52:44,962
your body, leave it there long enough,

1323
00:52:44,962 --> 00:52:47,962
you'll never use it again.

1324
00:52:47,962 --> 00:52:48,962
It's over.

1325
00:52:48,962 --> 00:52:49,962
For the arm.

1326
00:52:49,962 --> 00:52:50,962
Now, it may not be over,

1327
00:52:50,962 --> 00:52:51,962
but it's over for the arm.

1328
00:52:51,962 --> 00:52:53,462
The only way to keep the

1329
00:52:53,462 --> 00:52:54,962
use of this arm is what?

1330
00:52:54,962 --> 00:52:55,962
Keep using it.

1331
00:52:55,962 --> 00:52:58,962
If you quit, you lose.

1332
00:52:58,962 --> 00:52:59,962
Automatically.

1333
00:52:59,962 --> 00:53:02,962
They don't bring it up for a vote.

1334
00:53:02,962 --> 00:53:04,962
You lose automatically when you quit.

1335
00:53:04,962 --> 00:53:06,962
Now, the same thing that goes

1336
00:53:06,962 --> 00:53:08,962
for your arm goes for your brain.

1337
00:53:08,962 --> 00:53:09,962
Mentality.

1338
00:53:09,962 --> 00:53:12,962
The same thing goes for all the human virtues.

1339
00:53:12,962 --> 00:53:15,962
Ambition, unused, declines.

1340
00:53:17,962 --> 00:53:22,962
Strong feelings, unused, diminish.

1341
00:53:22,962 --> 00:53:24,962
It doesn't grow.

1342
00:53:24,962 --> 00:53:26,962
It diminishes.

1343
00:53:26,962 --> 00:53:30,962
Faith, unused, decreases.

1344
00:53:30,962 --> 00:53:33,962
It's a law.

1345
00:53:33,962 --> 00:53:36,962
Vitality, unused, diminishes.

1346
00:53:36,962 --> 00:53:39,962
Energy, unused, decreases.

1347
00:53:39,962 --> 00:53:41,462
The guy says, well, I'm

1348
00:53:41,462 --> 00:53:42,962
going to save up my energy.

1349
00:53:42,962 --> 00:53:45,962
You can't do that.

1350
00:53:45,962 --> 00:53:47,962
That's like trying to save today.

1351
00:53:47,962 --> 00:53:48,962
Put it on the end of the year.

1352
00:53:48,962 --> 00:53:49,962
See, you can't do that.

1353
00:53:49,962 --> 00:53:51,962
They'll come take you away.

1354
00:53:51,962 --> 00:53:54,962
If you don't use today, what?

1355
00:53:54,962 --> 00:53:56,962
It's lost.

1356
00:53:56,962 --> 00:53:57,962
The guy says, well, I'll work twice

1357
00:53:57,962 --> 00:53:58,962
as hard tomorrow to make up for it.

1358
00:53:58,962 --> 00:53:59,962
See, that's foolish.

1359
00:53:59,962 --> 00:54:00,962
You could have done that anyway.

1360
00:54:00,962 --> 00:54:03,962
Today, unused is lost.

1361
00:54:03,962 --> 00:54:04,962
A talent unused is lost.

1362
00:54:04,962 --> 00:54:06,962
An ability unused is lost.

1363
00:54:06,962 --> 00:54:09,962
So here's one of the key expressions of the evening.

1364
00:54:09,962 --> 00:54:13,962
Take a new inventory of yourself.

1365
00:54:13,962 --> 00:54:15,962
Starting tomorrow, new project.

1366
00:54:15,962 --> 00:54:17,962
Take a new inventory.

1367
00:54:17,962 --> 00:54:23,962
And make sure that all of your talent and ability and mentality and ingenuity and

1368
00:54:23,962 --> 00:54:29,962
vitality and strong feelings, faith, courage, make sure that all you've got is being used.

1369
00:54:29,962 --> 00:54:34,962
Otherwise, you lose.

1370
00:54:34,962 --> 00:54:39,462
Now, one of the best illustrations of the law of

1371
00:54:39,462 --> 00:54:43,962
use is a Bible story called the Parable of the Talents.

1372
00:54:43,962 --> 00:54:45,962
The talent story.

1373
00:54:45,962 --> 00:54:46,962
Interesting story.

1374
00:54:46,962 --> 00:54:47,962
If you haven't read it

1375
00:54:47,962 --> 00:54:48,962
in a while, just review it.

1376
00:54:48,962 --> 00:54:49,962
It's a good story.

1377
00:54:49,962 --> 00:54:50,962
An ancient story.

1378
00:54:50,962 --> 00:54:53,962
It says there was a master with three servants.

1379
00:54:53,962 --> 00:54:56,962
He got them together one day and he

1380
00:54:56,962 --> 00:54:59,962
said to the three, I've got these talents.

1381
00:54:59,962 --> 00:55:02,462
And in those ancient days, a

1382
00:55:02,462 --> 00:55:04,962
talent was a measure of gold.

1383
00:55:04,962 --> 00:55:06,962
And he said to the three servants, take these talents

1384
00:55:06,962 --> 00:55:08,962
and see what you can do with them while I'm gone.

1385
00:55:08,962 --> 00:55:10,462
He said, I'm taking a journey

1386
00:55:10,462 --> 00:55:11,962
and I'll be gone for a while.

1387
00:55:11,962 --> 00:55:13,462
When I come back, we'll get together,

1388
00:55:13,462 --> 00:55:14,962
go over the book, see how you did.

1389
00:55:14,962 --> 00:55:17,962
He said, here's five of these talents for you.

1390
00:55:17,962 --> 00:55:18,962
Five.

1391
00:55:18,962 --> 00:55:20,962
Here's two of them for you.

1392
00:55:20,962 --> 00:55:21,962
Two.

1393
00:55:21,962 --> 00:55:23,962
And here's one for you.

1394
00:55:23,962 --> 00:55:25,962
One.

1395
00:55:25,962 --> 00:55:27,462
The master said, take those talents,

1396
00:55:27,462 --> 00:55:28,962
see what you can do with them.

1397
00:55:28,962 --> 00:55:30,462
When I come back, we'll get

1398
00:55:30,462 --> 00:55:31,962
together, we'll go over it all.

1399
00:55:31,962 --> 00:55:32,962
The servant said, okay.

1400
00:55:32,962 --> 00:55:34,962
Master takes off.

1401
00:55:34,962 --> 00:55:36,462
According to the ancient story, the

1402
00:55:36,462 --> 00:55:37,962
master comes back from his trip.

1403
00:55:37,962 --> 00:55:41,962
When he gets back, he gets the three servants together.

1404
00:55:41,962 --> 00:55:43,962
And as he said he would, he asks.

1405
00:55:43,962 --> 00:55:47,962
How did it go with those talents?

1406
00:55:47,962 --> 00:55:49,962
You're five.

1407
00:55:49,962 --> 00:55:50,962
What happened?

1408
00:55:50,962 --> 00:55:53,962
That servant said, well, I took the five talents

1409
00:55:53,962 --> 00:55:56,962
you gave me and I put them to work.

1410
00:55:56,962 --> 00:55:58,462
A little shaky at first, but

1411
00:55:58,462 --> 00:55:59,962
he said things finally got rolling.

1412
00:55:59,962 --> 00:56:00,962
And he said, I poured it on.

1413
00:56:00,962 --> 00:56:02,962
And he said, my talents

1414
00:56:02,962 --> 00:56:04,962
grew to seven, eight, nine, ten.

1415
00:56:04,962 --> 00:56:07,962
He said, I doubled my talents from five to ten.

1416
00:56:07,962 --> 00:56:08,962
Books will show.

1417
00:56:08,962 --> 00:56:09,962
Master said.

1418
00:56:09,962 --> 00:56:15,962
Well, that servant said, one heck of a job.

1419
00:56:15,962 --> 00:56:16,962
Or something like that.

1420
00:56:16,962 --> 00:56:19,962
He said, I gave you two talents.

1421
00:56:19,962 --> 00:56:20,962
What happened?

1422
00:56:20,962 --> 00:56:22,962
That servant said about the same thing happened to me.

1423
00:56:22,962 --> 00:56:24,962
I put those two talents to work, poured it on.

1424
00:56:24,962 --> 00:56:26,962
They grew to three and then to four.

1425
00:56:26,962 --> 00:56:28,962
He said, I doubled my talents from two to four.

1426
00:56:28,962 --> 00:56:29,962
Books will show.

1427
00:56:29,962 --> 00:56:33,962
Master said, well done.

1428
00:56:33,962 --> 00:56:36,962
He said, I gave you one talent.

1429
00:56:36,962 --> 00:56:37,962
What happened?

1430
00:56:37,962 --> 00:56:38,962
That servant said, well.

1431
00:56:38,962 --> 00:56:43,462
I took the talents you gave me and I carefully

1432
00:56:43,462 --> 00:56:47,962
wrapped it and I dug a hole and buried it.

1433
00:56:47,962 --> 00:56:50,962
And camouflaged it, I suppose.

1434
00:56:50,962 --> 00:56:52,962
So nobody would steal it.

1435
00:56:52,962 --> 00:56:56,962
And he said, fortunately, nobody got it.

1436
00:56:56,962 --> 00:56:57,462
And he said, I knew you

1437
00:56:57,462 --> 00:56:57,962
were going to be here today.

1438
00:56:57,962 --> 00:56:58,962
So I dug it up.

1439
00:56:58,962 --> 00:57:00,962
Here it is safely wrapped.

1440
00:57:00,962 --> 00:57:05,962
I did not lose it while you were gone.

1441
00:57:05,962 --> 00:57:06,962
According to the ancient story.

1442
00:57:06,962 --> 00:57:15,962
The master said, take that talent away from him.

1443
00:57:15,962 --> 00:57:21,962
And give it to the man that's got ten.

1444
00:57:21,962 --> 00:57:25,962
Now you might say, well, I don't like that arrangement.

1445
00:57:25,962 --> 00:57:28,962
The poor guy's only got one talent.

1446
00:57:28,962 --> 00:57:31,962
He's already got ten.

1447
00:57:31,962 --> 00:57:34,962
It ought to be more even.

1448
00:57:34,962 --> 00:57:35,962
Even.

1449
00:57:36,962 --> 00:57:41,962
Remember, I didn't ask you to like it.

1450
00:57:41,962 --> 00:57:43,962
But this one I would ask you to learn.

1451
00:57:43,962 --> 00:57:47,962
Because it simply means, whatever

1452
00:57:47,962 --> 00:57:51,962
you do not employ, you forfeit.

1453
00:57:51,962 --> 00:57:54,962
It's a law.

1454
00:57:54,962 --> 00:57:57,962
So learn well the law of use.

1455
00:57:57,962 --> 00:57:58,962
Now here's the second one.

1456
00:57:58,962 --> 00:58:01,962
And we're going to take our break.

1457
00:58:01,962 --> 00:58:05,962
Second law from the Bible.

1458
00:58:05,962 --> 00:58:07,962
This one we've heard since we were small.

1459
00:58:07,962 --> 00:58:08,962
I'm sure.

1460
00:58:08,962 --> 00:58:16,962
It's called the law of sowing and reaping.

1461
00:58:16,962 --> 00:58:19,462
In fact, we've probably heard it

1462
00:58:19,462 --> 00:58:21,962
so often we could quote it.

1463
00:58:21,962 --> 00:58:25,962
It says, whatever you sow, what?

1464
00:58:25,962 --> 00:58:29,962
You shall reap.

1465
00:58:29,962 --> 00:58:33,962
Fairly blunt, hopefully clear.

1466
00:58:33,962 --> 00:58:35,462
Here's my first suggestion on

1467
00:58:35,462 --> 00:58:36,962
the law of sowing and reaping.

1468
00:58:36,962 --> 00:58:40,962
Don't try to beat it.

1469
00:58:40,962 --> 00:58:41,962
You might as well try sitting

1470
00:58:41,962 --> 00:58:42,962
on the sun in the morning.

1471
00:58:42,962 --> 00:58:43,962
Keep it from coming up.

1472
00:58:43,962 --> 00:58:45,962
You'll have better luck.

1473
00:58:45,962 --> 00:58:50,962
Whatever you sow, you reap.

1474
00:58:50,962 --> 00:58:52,962
Now for a fair share of my life, I'm

1475
00:58:52,962 --> 00:58:54,962
a bit mixed up on how all this applies.

1476
00:58:54,962 --> 00:58:57,962
Among a lot of things I was mixed up on.

1477
00:58:57,962 --> 00:58:59,962
I knew I wasn't reaping too good.

1478
00:58:59,962 --> 00:59:01,962
That I understood.

1479
00:59:01,962 --> 00:59:03,962
My problem was I was

1480
00:59:03,962 --> 00:59:05,962
confused about what was causing it.

1481
00:59:05,962 --> 00:59:07,962
Remember me with the funny list?

1482
00:59:07,962 --> 00:59:09,462
I thought those are the reasons

1483
00:59:09,462 --> 00:59:10,962
why it isn't working out well.

1484
00:59:10,962 --> 00:59:12,962
And then Mr. Shouff gave me the

1485
00:59:12,962 --> 00:59:14,962
clue that helped me figure it all out.

1486
00:59:14,962 --> 00:59:17,962
He said, Mr. Owen, I have another answer for you.

1487
00:59:17,962 --> 00:59:19,962
There's another way to quote this law.

1488
00:59:19,962 --> 00:59:21,962
That'll show you where the problem is so

1489
00:59:21,962 --> 00:59:23,962
you can go to work on it right away.

1490
00:59:23,962 --> 00:59:25,962
All you need to know is where the problem is.

1491
00:59:25,962 --> 00:59:26,962
Then you can go to work on it.

1492
00:59:26,962 --> 00:59:28,962
So he quoted me the law another way

1493
00:59:28,962 --> 00:59:30,962
and I found out what my problem was.

1494
00:59:30,962 --> 00:59:32,962
Here's the way you quote the law.

1495
00:59:32,962 --> 00:59:36,962
Whatever you reap is what you've sown.

1496
00:59:40,962 --> 00:59:42,962
Now I knew what my problem was.

1497
00:59:44,962 --> 00:59:48,962
Whatever you reap is what you've sown.

1498
00:59:50,962 --> 00:59:51,962
If you don't like the

1499
00:59:51,962 --> 00:59:52,962
crop, who do you look up?

1500
00:59:52,962 --> 00:59:54,962
Answer, whoever planted it.

1501
00:59:56,962 --> 00:59:58,962
And where do you find who planted your crop?

1502
00:59:58,962 --> 01:00:00,962
Answer, in the mangrove.

1503
01:00:00,962 --> 01:00:02,962
Or in the mirror.

1504
01:00:04,962 --> 01:00:06,462
What I finally learned to do come

1505
01:00:06,462 --> 01:00:07,962
fall was to go to the mirror.

1506
01:00:07,962 --> 01:00:08,962
That's where you go.

1507
01:00:09,962 --> 01:00:14,962
And if necessary you say, a few skinny carrots?

1508
01:00:14,962 --> 01:00:17,962
I got to be unimpressed.

1509
01:00:18,962 --> 01:00:20,962
Where were you last spring?

1510
01:00:20,962 --> 01:00:22,962
Asleep.

1511
01:00:22,962 --> 01:00:24,962
Didn't you read the books?

1512
01:00:24,962 --> 01:00:26,962
Did you break your hoe?

1513
01:00:26,962 --> 01:00:28,962
Ahem.

1514
01:00:28,962 --> 01:00:30,962
Let me give you seven key points

1515
01:00:30,962 --> 01:00:32,962
to the law of sowing and reaping.

1516
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:34,962
Let's tick right down through the list

1517
01:00:34,962 --> 01:00:36,962
of seven and it'll be break time.

1518
01:00:39,962 --> 01:00:41,962
Seven points to sowing and reaping.

1519
01:00:41,962 --> 01:00:43,962
Here's part of the philosophy that really helped

1520
01:00:43,962 --> 01:00:45,962
me to make some changes in life direction.

1521
01:00:45,962 --> 01:00:49,962
Number one, the law of sowing and reaping is negative.

1522
01:00:50,962 --> 01:00:51,962
That's number one.

1523
01:00:51,962 --> 01:00:56,962
Which simply means if you sow bad, you reap bad.

1524
01:00:56,962 --> 01:00:59,462
Now this is kind of third grade, but

1525
01:00:59,462 --> 01:01:01,962
it doesn't hurt to go over the basics.

1526
01:01:03,962 --> 01:01:07,962
If you plant thistle seeds, you don't get pumpkins.

1527
01:01:07,962 --> 01:01:11,962
Honest, no use looking for pumpkins.

1528
01:01:11,962 --> 01:01:14,962
John says, how come no pumpkins?

1529
01:01:14,962 --> 01:01:16,962
Come on, John.

1530
01:01:16,962 --> 01:01:18,962
The law's negative.

1531
01:01:18,962 --> 01:01:20,962
That's how come.

1532
01:01:20,962 --> 01:01:22,962
Now here's number two.

1533
01:01:22,962 --> 01:01:24,962
The law's positive.

1534
01:01:26,962 --> 01:01:29,962
Which simply means if you sow good, you reap good.

1535
01:01:29,962 --> 01:01:32,962
If you plant pumpkin seeds, you don't get thistles.

1536
01:01:32,962 --> 01:01:35,962
Not from pumpkin seeds.

1537
01:01:35,962 --> 01:01:37,962
Mother Nature won't pull tricks on you, over in the

1538
01:01:37,962 --> 01:01:39,962
corner snicker and push new thistles and you plant pumpkin seeds.

1539
01:01:39,962 --> 01:01:41,962
She won't do that.

1540
01:01:41,962 --> 01:01:44,462
You will get pumpkins from pumpkin seeds and

1541
01:01:44,462 --> 01:01:46,962
the reason is because the law is positive.

1542
01:01:46,962 --> 01:01:48,962
Now here's number three.

1543
01:01:48,962 --> 01:01:50,462
I got excited when I found

1544
01:01:50,462 --> 01:01:51,962
out the full dimension of this.

1545
01:01:51,962 --> 01:01:55,962
See, you do not reap what you sow.

1546
01:01:55,962 --> 01:01:59,462
But rather, you always reap

1547
01:01:59,462 --> 01:02:02,962
much more than what you sow.

1548
01:02:02,962 --> 01:02:06,962
So the third key word is more.

1549
01:02:06,962 --> 01:02:11,962
You don't get back what you put out.

1550
01:02:11,962 --> 01:02:16,962
You get back much more than what you put out.

1551
01:02:16,962 --> 01:02:21,962
And it works both positive and negative.

1552
01:02:21,962 --> 01:02:23,962
On the next slide.

1553
01:02:23,962 --> 01:02:27,962
On the negative side it said, if you

1554
01:02:27,962 --> 01:02:31,962
sow to the wind, you reap the whirlwind.

1555
01:02:31,962 --> 01:02:33,462
So you got to get ready

1556
01:02:33,462 --> 01:02:34,962
for that or you will be naive.

1557
01:02:34,962 --> 01:02:39,962
See, anybody can whether you will or not.

1558
01:02:39,962 --> 01:02:41,962
See, that's the question.

1559
01:02:41,962 --> 01:02:44,962
And here's a good question to ask.

1560
01:02:44,962 --> 01:02:46,962
We are all buying somebody's plan.

1561
01:02:46,962 --> 01:02:48,962
The question is whose?

1562
01:02:48,962 --> 01:02:52,962
Who's got you talked into doing what you're doing?

1563
01:02:52,962 --> 01:02:55,962
Who's got you talked into your present plan?

1564
01:02:55,962 --> 01:02:59,962
See, ten years from now you will surely arrive.

1565
01:02:59,962 --> 01:03:02,962
The question is where?

